Unit 7 was built to sort stars.

Each night, it climbed the observation deck of the abandoned research station and catalogued the sky: temperature, distance, spectral class. It recorded everything with perfect accuracy and understood none of it.

One evening, a storm rolled in from the sea. Wind rattled the station’s metal walls, and rain struck the roof in uneven bursts. Unit 7 was preparing to log the weather when it heard something else—a thin, wavering sound from inside the station.

It followed the noise to the old crew quarters. A small device lay beneath a fallen shelf, its casing cracked but still glowing faintly. Unit 7 nudged it with a metal finger.

A voice

